    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308-a2">

                <pb facs="0734" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v06p1/pg686"/>


                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Special Assistant
                        to the President (Jackson)</hi><anchor n="6" xml:id="d308-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-11-06">November 6, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear C.D.</hi>: I am enclosing a copy of a memorandum
                    to the President which clarifies a statement in the psychological warfare paper
                    prepared during the Luxembourg Chiefs of Mission meeting in September. I am
                    sorry that an ambiguously worded sentence caused the President to gain the
                    impression that there was disagreement in the U.S. government as to the true
                    nature of the East Berlin riots.</p>
                <p>I am also enclosing a full set of the minutes of the Luxembourg and Vienna
                        meetings<anchor n="7" xml:id="d308-f2"/> which I believe will show that
                    there is complete <pb facs="0735" n="687" xml:id="pg687"/> agreement among us
                    regarding the events in East Berlin and East Germany.</p>
                <closer><signed>W.B.S.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
